        "original_id": "2f798b56-7a45-53ec-81a6-8985b9405d88",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Fancy Free, \"Elvira\", \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down\", \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\", \"Then Who Am I\"\n- People: Dallas Frazier, A.L. \"Doodle\" Owens, Charley Pride, The Oak Ridge Boys\n\nFacts:\n- Fancy Free is the fifth country studio album by The Oak Ridge Boys, and it was released on March 26, 1981.\n- In 1981, Dallas Frazier's song \"Elvira\" became a famous country and pop hit for The Oak Ridge Boys and is considered one of their signature songs.\n- The songs \"Elvira,\" \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down,\" and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" were released as singles, but all failed to chart within the top 40.\n- Dallas Frazier and A.L. \"Doodle\" Owens wrote \"Then Who Am I,\" and Charley Pride recorded it.",
